NEARS-2184 QA — regression_bug (PRE-EXISTING, not caused by this diff): a 403 on
/api/v1/stores/details/{id} is swallowed with NO paired AppLogger.failure line.

Observed twice on emulator-5556, on two different app processes, while browsing the cart /
store surfaces:
  08-16 03:02:15.117  23920  I flutter : [NET] endpoint=/api/v1/stores/details/17 http_status=403
  08-16 03:03:23.200  24827  I flutter : [NET] endpoint=/api/v1/stores/details/17 http_status=403
Neither is followed by a [FAIL]/[ERR] line (grep over each pid's full flutter-tag buffer for
"\[ERR\]|\[FAIL\]" returns only the unrelated common-condition entry).

Cause is NOT the module header — identical response with and without it:
  $ curl -H 'zoneId: [1]' -H 'moduleId: 1' 'http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/stores/details/17'
  403 {"errors":[{"code":"out_of_zone","message":"Store not available in your zone"}]}
  $ curl -H 'zoneId: [1]'                  'http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/stores/details/17'
  403 {"errors":[{"code":"out_of_zone","message":"Store not available in your zone"}]}

So: an out-of-zone store detail fetch fails on the wire and the app logs only the routine
[NET] status line — a silent failure path per docs/platform/logging-contract.md (every
failure path needs a paired AppLogger.failure). Pre-existing behaviour, reachable
independently of NEARS-2184; filed for the PO's backlog, not against this change.
